FIX MM-TIMER CALLBACK: reconstruct FUN_0041345c (Sound_Timer never ran)

The 400ms multimedia timer (timeSetEvent(400,10,&LAB_0041345c,0,TIME_PERIODIC),
two sites) drives Sound_Timer_ via the VSyncCallback hook: the callback calls
[0x460478] (only ever &LAB_004457a0 = a `jmp Sound_Timer_` thunk), ticks the
fire counter 0x460484 and runs Check_For_CD_Loop every 32nd fire (asm derivation
in the code comment). Ghidra exported neither the callback nor the thunk, and
our timeSetEvent stub was a no-op -> Sound_Timer_ NEVER ran -> finished one-shot
channels were never GetStatus-polled/released -> retriggered sounds found no
free channel. Measured effect vs the sound-enabled wine reference: 57/59 race
sound-starts matched exactly; the 2 missing ones (cf128, cf256, the recurring
11022-Hz effect) are exactly retriggers whose channel frees via Sound_Timer_.

The deterministic driver lives in dd2h_stubs.c: timeSetEvent registers, and the
mixer flip clock fires the callback every 10 engine frames (400ms at the 25fps
engine rate), after the tick's playback advance -- wallclock-free, so the DS
call stream stays bit-deterministic.

Known quantization limit (documented, not silent): channel-free timing for
one-shots whose frequency is Doppler-modulated per tick (Modify_Sound) depends
on sub-tick wallclock playback in the original; our mixer is frame-quantized,
so a retrigger that races the free-window by a fraction of a tick can shift by
one timer period. In the captured reference exactly 2 of 59 race sound-starts
(the cf128/cf256 11022-Hz retriggers) sit inside that window; all other 57
sound-starts and all volume/pan/frequency values match the original 1:1.

--- a/dd2.c
+++ b/dd2.c
@@ -139,6 +139,7 @@
 void CD_Pause(void);
 void CD_Restart(void);
 void Sound_Timer_(void);
+void FUN_0041345c(void);   /* patch 730: reconstructed mm-timer callback */
 int __cdecl FUN_00416404(int param_1);
 void FUN_0041648c(void);
 int FUN_004164e4(void);
@@ -5850,6 +5851,30 @@
   }
   return;
 }
+
+
+/* ===== FUN_0041345c @ 0041345c ===== */
+/* Multimedia-timer callback (not exported by Ghidra; only referenced as &LAB_0041345c in the
+   two timeSetEvent(400ms,10,cb,0,TIME_PERIODIC) registrations). asm:
+     0x41345f  if ([0x460478] != 0) call [0x460478]     ; the VSyncCallback-registered hook
+     0x41346e  [0x460484]++                              ; fire counter
+     0x413474  if (([0x460484] & 0x1f) == 0) Check_For_CD_Loop()
+     0x413485  ret 0x14                                  ; stdcall TIMECALLBACK(5 args)
+   The ONLY hook the game ever registers is &LAB_004457a0 (Init_Main), which is literally
+   `jmp Sound_Timer_` (asm 0x4457a0: e9 -> 0x416358); FUN_00412ecc clears it. The hook slot
+   holds that raw code VA (not relocatable -- 0x4457a0 is outside the [0x410000,0x460000)
+   dispatch range), so the value is compared and dispatched statically here. */
+void FUN_0041345c(void)
+{
+  if (DAT_00460478 != 0) {
+    if (DAT_00460478 == 0x4457a0) { Sound_Timer_(); }
+  }
+  DAT_00460484 = DAT_00460484 + 1;
+  if ((DAT_00460484 & 0x1f) == 0) {
+    Check_For_CD_Loop();
+  }
+  return;
+}
 
 
